# Development-only files, kept out of the packed mod.
#
# Entries are exact relative paths -- modkit matches the whole path, not a
# directory prefix -- so a new test file needs its own line here.
#
# `modkit pack` zips everything under the mod directory, so anything listed
# here is also left out of the release, which is what we want: the tests need a
# gen1recomp checkout to run against and are no part of the installed mod.
#
# tools/ is the same kind of thing: four Python scripts that need the ROM and
# a gen1recomp checkout to do anything at all.  Three of them are how the fact
# that matters most about this port was established -- that FRLG's trainer class
# and trainer front pic are different number spaces -- and the fourth is the
# vendored release builder the CI workflow calls.  They are worth keeping in the
# source tree, but an installed mod has no use for them.
tests/dp3_speaker_test.lua
tests/dp3_geometry_test.lua
tests/dp3_load_test.lua
tests/dp3_menu_test.lua
tests/launcher_update_test.lua
tools/dump_class_names.py
tools/dump_class_pics.py
tools/dump_trainers.py
tools/build_release.py
tools/changelog_section.py

# CHANGELOG.md and README.md, for now.
#
# Neither is read out of an INSTALLED mod: the launcher's "What's New?" renders
# the GitHub Release body, which the workflow extracts from the source tree,
# not from the payload, and nothing else in the engine opens either file.  They
# stay in the source tree, so the release workflow still publishes CHANGELOG.md's
# "## <version>" section as the body.
#
# CHANGELOG.md is also the file a stale read-only copy in a previous install
# blocks an update on --
#
#   could not write CHANGELOG.md: ... (permission denied)
#
# -- because Windows cannot delete a read-only file, so the installer can
# neither clear the old tree nor write the new file.  Keeping both out of the
# payload lets an update step past a stale copy of either.
CHANGELOG.md
README.md

# Player-supplied art.
#
# CustomArt/ is the documented route for giving a portrait to somebody the ROM
# has none for (see CustomArt/README.md), and every file a PLAYER drops here is
# their own business -- commit it or don't, it is not part of the mod.
#
# This mod ships no art at all: every portrait is cut at runtime out of the
# engine's own extraction of the player's ROM, so there is nothing here that
# needs to ride along.  CustomArt/README.md is deliberately NOT listed -- it is
# the how-to and it ships.  Add a line here for anything you drop in locally so
# a personal experiment never ends up in the package.

# A guard, not a description of the tree.
#
# The tree itself carries no build output: the release zip is built by CI from
# the tagged tree and attached to the GitHub Release, never committed (see
# .github/workflows/release.yml, and .gitignore).  These two lines are here for
# the case where somebody builds a release by hand *into the repo root* -- both
# `modkit pack` and tools/build_release.py walk the whole tree, so a stray
# artifact gets folded into the next build.
#
# Exact paths, like every other entry here, so a version bump means renaming
# them.  `tests/launcher_update_test.lua` fails if they stop matching the
# manifest's id and version, which is the reminder.
gen3-dialogue-portraits-1.2.2.modpkg
gen3-dialogue-portraits-1.2.2.zip
